/-! # Einstein–Maxwell certificate and generic lemmas (ATLAS-IV-01)

`EinsteinMaxwellCertificate g ginv F U` (class B) bundles the obligations of the roadmap §2: open nonempty
domain, symmetric metric with a genuine inverse, Lorentz signature, `C^∞` metric / inverse / field
components (order `∞ = ((⊤ : ℕ∞) : WithTop ℕ∞)`, not `ω`), antisymmetric `F`, and the three residuals
`E = 0`, `J = 0`, `H = 0`. Each field must be discharged by a theorem; nothing here assumes a residual.

Generic results (no instance data):
* `trace_ginv_g`, `trace_emStress`: in 4D the Maxwell stress tensor is trace-free.
* `faradayCyclic_eq_zero_of_eqOn_extD`: if `F = dA` on an open set with `A` of class `C^∞`, then
  `H = 0` there (symmetry of mixed partials, `pd_pd_symm`).
* `ofVacuum` / `toVacuum`: with `F = 0` the certificate is equivalent to `VacuumCertificate`. -/

open scoped ContDiff

namespace ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell

/-- Einstein–Maxwell certificate for `(g, F)` on `U` in four dimensions (signature `(-,+,+,+)`). -/
structure EinsteinMaxwellCertificate (g ginv : Metric 4) (F : TwoForm 4) (U : Set (Pt 4)) : Prop where
  isOpen : IsOpen U
  nonempty : U.Nonempty
  symm : ∀ x ∈ U, ∀ i j, g i j x = g j i x
  inv : ∀ x ∈ U, metricMatrix ginv x * metricMatrix g x = 1
  smooth : ∀ i j, ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (g i j) U
  smooth_inv : ∀ i j, ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (ginv i j) U
  smooth_F : ∀ i j, ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (F i j) U
  antisymm : ∀ x ∈ U, ∀ i j, F i j x = -F j i x
  lorentz : ∀ x ∈ U, IsLorentzian (metricMatrix g x)
  einstein : ∀ x ∈ U, ∀ i j, einsteinMaxwell g ginv F i j x = 0
  maxwell : ∀ x ∈ U, ∀ j, maxwellDiv g ginv F j x = 0
  closed : ∀ x ∈ U, ∀ i j k, faradayCyclic F i j k x = 0

namespace EinsteinMaxwellCertificate

variable {g ginv : Metric 4} {F : TwoForm 4} {U : Set (Pt 4)}

end EinsteinMaxwellCertificate

